.TH WLIST-SHOW 1 "17 November 2026" "version 0.3.0"
.SH NAME
wlist-show \- displays the list and other data.
.SH SYNOPSIS
wlist show [path/to/database]
[--content <content type> | -c <content type>]
[--item-id <id> | -i <id> ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
show list and other details.
.PP
Those details can either be:
.RS
.IP 
details about items
.IP
the items in the list.
.IP
notes
.RE
.PP
When view the item list, which is the default, 
you cannot specify a particular item, 
unlike if you were to view the notes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -c <content type>, --content <content type>
Determines what to show.
.PP
The value can be either **items** or **notes**
.PP
Items is default and will show the registry,
while notes will show the notes and, 
if an item id is supplied, show notes attached to an item.
.TP
.B -i <id>, --item-id <id>
The item to be looked up.
.PP
This can only be used when viewing notes.
.SH AUTHOR
Bryce Campbell (tonyhawk2100@gmail.com)
.SH EXAMPLES
View list:
.RS
wlist show
.RE
.PP
View notes:
.RS
wlist show -c notes
.RE
.PP
View notes connected to item:
.RS
wlist show -c -i FF04C3DC-F0FE-472E-8737-0F4034C049F0
.RE